**Main bug:** `forEach` ignores async callbacks' promises. Function returns `users` before any fetch finishes, so caller gets `[]`.

**Other bugs:**
- Result order is not guaranteed. `push` happens in completion order, not `ids` order.
- No error handling. Rejected fetch becomes unhandled rejection, not caught by caller. Also `fetch` does not reject on 404/500; `res.ok` is never checked.

**Fix:**
```js
async function loadUsers(ids) {
  return Promise.all(ids.map(async id => {
    const res = await fetch(`/api/users/${id}`);
    if (!res.ok) throw new Error(`Failed to load user ${id}: ${res.status}`);
    return res.json();
  }));
}
```

`Promise.all` keeps order and rejects on first failure. Use `Promise.allSettled` if partial results are OK.

